  "htmlContent": "<p>We start with how we define vectors in plane or space.\nFor vectors in plane <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> we have the following mathematical definition:</p>\n<span class=\"katex-error\" title=\"ParseError: KaTeX parse error: Expected &#x27;EOF&#x27;, got &#x27;\\end&#x27; at position 8: x \\\\\ny\n\\̲e̲n̲d̲{bmatrix},\n\\qua…\" style=\"color:#cc0000\">x \\\\\ny\n\\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad x,y \\space \\in \\space \\mathbb{R}</span>\n<p>And for vectors in space <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}^3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<span class=\"katex-error\" title=\"ParseError: KaTeX parse error: Expected &#x27;EOF&#x27;, got &#x27;\\end&#x27; at position 13: x \\\\\ny \\\\\nz\n\\̲e̲n̲d̲{bmatrix},\n\\qua…\" style=\"color:#cc0000\">x \\\\\ny \\\\\nz\n\\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad x,y,z \\space \\in \\space \\mathbb{R}</span>\n<p>Here, we will not go into detail about the operations that can be performed on vectors. These generally include</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vector Addition</li>\n<li>Scalar Multiplication</li>\n<li>Vector multiplication (Dot Product, Cross Product)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.1 Linear Combinations</h2>\n<p>Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>⃗</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{\\vec{v}_1, \\vec{v}_2, ..., \\vec{v}_p\\} \\space \\in \\mathbb{R}^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.714em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mat